    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"control_flow - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\":\n    \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/control_flow.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [control_flow()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-function} | EdgeCase\n  description: The control flow graph of a short function.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [control_flow()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-function} | EdgeCase\n  description: The control flow graph of a short function.\ntitle: >-\n  [control_flow()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-function}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: The control flow graph of a short function.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nThe control flow graph of a short function.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/example_networks.py#L2469-L2551){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\ncontrol_flow()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\nThe control flow graph a compiler would build for this Python function, which averages the\nabsolute values of a list, stopping early once the running total passes a limit:\n\n```python\ndef mean_abs(values, limit):\n    total, n = 0, 0\n    for x in values:\n        if x < 0:\n            x = -x\n        total += x\n        n += 1\n        if total > limit:\n            break\n    if n == 0:\n        return None\n    return total / n\n```\n\nEach node is a basic block, a run of code that always executes from start to finish, and\neach edge a possible jump from one block to the next. Every run of the function follows a\npath from `entry` to `exit`. It's the example for the analyses compilers do: dominators,\ndominance frontiers, loops and depth-first edge types.\n\nNetwork Properties:\n\n- 11 nodes (basic blocks, labeled by a name for what they do)\n- 14 edges (possible jumps)\n- Directed, unweighted, with one cycle (the loop)\n\nNode Attributes:\n\n- `code`: the block's source code, such as `\"if x < 0:\"`; empty for `exit`\n- `pos`: an `(x, y)` position for drawing the graph, left to right from `entry` to `exit`\n\nEdge Attributes:\n\n- `branch`: which way a test went to take the jump, `\"true\"` or `\"false\"` for an `if`,\n  and `\"next\"` or `\"done\"` for the `for` loop; missing where control falls through\n\nWhat to Look For:\n\n- **One loop.** The five blocks from `loop` to `limit test` form the only strongly\n  connected component of more than one block, and the jump from `limit test` back to\n  `loop` is what closes it.\n- **Dominators.** Every path from `entry` to `add` passes through `sign test`, but not\n  through `negate`, which only runs for negative values, so `sign test` is the immediate\n  dominator of `add`. And every path to `exit` passes through `empty test`.\n- **Where paths merge.** The dominance frontier of `negate` is `add`, where the paths with\n  and without `x = -x` meet again: the place a compiler in SSA form puts a φ-function for\n  `x`. The frontier of `loop` is `loop` itself, the sign of a loop header.\n- **Two ways out of the loop.** The loop ends when the values run out (`done`) or at the\n  `break`, and both paths lead to `empty test`, which `loop` dominates.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The control flow graph.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nDraw the graph from `entry` to `exit`, with the branch on each jump:\n\n::: {#90a04f99 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ncfg = ec.control_flow()\n\ncfg.plot(layout=\"pos\", label_by=\"label\", edge_label_by=\"branch\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"po